  "new_v0_7_claims": [
    "bounded quasi-polynomial residue profiles admit a canonical evaluation linear map into complex sequences",
    "positive affine sectioning sends a degree-d period-T quasi-polynomial profile to another profile with the same T and d via explicit affine polynomial substitution",
    "eventual agreement with a quasi-polynomial tail preserves the same threshold N under every positive affine section",
    "the common coordinate source (Fin N -> C) x DegreeBoundedProfile T d has exact finrank N + T(d+1)",
    "the range CommonHull N T d has finrank at most N + T(d+1)",
    "every element of CommonHull N T d has an eventual quasi-polynomial tail with the same N,T,d bounds",
    "CommonHull N T d is invariant under every positive affine section n -> mn+r",
    "from BellDownstreamInterface a, every positive affine section of a lies in the same CommonHull N T d",
    "therefore every depth and address of every positive radix lies in one common hull independent of radix, depth, and address",
    "there exists such a common hull with finrank bounded by N + T(d+1)"
  ],
  "explicit_boundaries": [
    "Bell generalized Cobham theorem remains external and is not formalized",
    "Bell Theorem 1.5 root-of-unity rationality is checked only in its integer-valued two-multiplicatively-independent-base regular scope",
    "Bell Theorem 1.4 by itself gives a linear recurrence over a commutative ring and is not silently promoted to root-of-unity rationality",
    "the rational-root-of-unity generating-function to eventual quasi-polynomial normalization is an external interface step in v0.7",
    "the internal common-hull theorem is over complex-valued sequences satisfying BellDownstreamInterface explicitly",
    "v0.7 does not prove every complex-valued two-base regular sequence satisfies BellDownstreamInterface",
    "v0.6 rank/nullity remains scoped to the saved finite complex projector-factorized affine normal form",
    "the naive base-independent integral normal form remains false and is not revived",
    "Lean verification does not establish literature novelty or priority"
  ],
  "external_inputs": [
    {
      "name": "Jason P. Bell, A Generalization of Cobham\u2019s Theorem for Regular Sequences, Theorem 1.5",
      "status": "external / checked primary source / not formalized",
      "use_boundary": "integer-valued k- and l-regular sequence with multiplicatively independent positive k,l -> rational generating function with all poles roots of unity"
